cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the SSO crossover catalogue, please cite it
  using the metadata below; a journal article is in preparation (see
  preferred-citation once published).
title: "Crossover Atlas: crossover points of satellite repeat ground tracks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vázquez"
    given-names: "Rafael"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Sevilla"
  - family-names: "Tesón Muñoz"
    given-names: "Eva"
  - family-names: "Montero Miñán"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-16"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Interactive catalogue and verification scripts for the crossover
  (self-intersection) structure of satellite repeat ground tracks: exact
  crossover counts via a colleague-matrix all-roots solver, critical
  inclinations and bifurcation structure, J2 invariance, an eccentric
  O(e^2) extension, and a catalogue of 329 repeat sun-synchronous orbits.
keywords:
  - repeat ground track
  - crossover points
  - astrodynamics
  - sun-synchronous orbits
  - critical inclination
repository-code: "https://github.com/redstovely/crossover-atlas"
url: "https://redstovely.github.io/crossover-atlas/"
